Description
This bounty is for developing and adding PopDEX Perpetual connectors to the official Hummingbot open-source codebase.

PopDEX is a trader-first perp DEX built for capital efficiency, execution quality, and 100% protocol value return to real contributors.

The connector must support PopDEX’s API architecture, including signed transactions, account abstraction (account index), and WebSocket streaming.

PopDEX API documentation:
https://popdex.xyz/docs/product-docs/intro

https://popdex.xyz/docs/api/intro

Hummingbot CLOB connector documentation:
https://hummingbot.org/connectors/clob/

Hummingbot connector debug guide:
https://hummingbot.org/developers/connectors/debug/

Hummingbot contribution guidelines:
https://github.com/hummingbot/hummingbot/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md

🎯 Bounty Goals
Build and maintain official Hummingbot connectors for:

PopDEX Perpetual
Ensure compatibility with Hummingbot v2.1+ connector standards

Add Candles (if available)

Connector docs to include for hummingbot-site repo

Add full unit and integration test coverage

Work with the PopDEX team to validate API usage and behavior. PopDEX Team TG Group - https://t.me/+bLR7RpCN0yg2NmMx

✅ Deliverables & Acceptance Criteria
Connector Implementation
The PopDEX Perpetual connectors must include:

Core Trading Functionality
Place limit and market orders via signed transactions
Cancel and modify orders
Fetch order status and trade history
Handle client order IDs
Account & Balance
Fetch account balances and positions
Support sub-accounts (account index model)
Handle collateral and margin (for perps)
Perpetual Features
Funding rate handling (https://popdex.xyz/docs/api/market/Get-Current-Funding-Rate)
Position tracking and PnL
Margin requirements and liquidation logic awareness
Market Data
Orderbook snapshots and updates
Trade streams
Ticker data
WebSocket Integration
Subscribe to:

Orderbook updates
Trades
User events (orders, fills, positions)
Code & PR Requirements
Code must follow Hummingbot connector patterns and naming conventions
Submitted via a single pull request to the Hummingbot repository
Must pass all CI checks
Must follow contribution guidelines:
https://github.com/hummingbot/hummingbot/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md
Reviewed and approved by Hummingbot maintainers

📞 Collaboration With PopDEX
Developer may need to:

Work with PopDEX team on:

API signing and auth flows
Edge cases (nonce desync, failed tx, batching)

Validate:
Order execution correctness
Funding & liquidation behavior
WebSocket message formats
🚀 Impact
This connector enables Hummingbot users to trade on a next-generation ZK exchange, combining:

CEX-level performance
On-chain verification
This is a high-impact integration due to PopDEX’s unique architecture and growing ecosystem.

